-- 288: assert_lifecycle_phase_distribution — the step's logic variables are copied to step-owned names (C6-1, commit ②).
--
-- McDonald's Airtight V3 (Spec 132 §core.8 (R-DE), R-DF EXTERNALIZED; defect ALPD-D1; the copy form of migrations 270 /
-- 273-275, Spec 132 §x-stages.2 (R-EQ) / R-FC): step-owned logic variables are `<slug>_<name>`. The converted step
-- (scripts/quality/assert-lifecycle-phase-distribution.descriptor.json) reads 197 names:
--   9 scalars   lifecycle_<x>                 -> assert_lifecycle_phase_distribution_<x>
--   110 band mins lifecycle_seq_band_<n>_min    -> assert_lifecycle_phase_distribution_seq_band_<n>_min
--   77 band maxs lifecycle_seq_band_<n>_max    -> assert_lifecycle_phase_distribution_seq_band_<n>_max
--   1 new       assert_lifecycle_phase_distribution_max_detail_keys (default 50; was the SEQ_VIOLATIONS_CAP literal, R-EP)
-- The 33 band maxima seeded NULL ("no upper bound": the catalog rows_count NULL/0 seqs, migration 148 :86) are NOT
-- copied: a logic variable is a finite number (scripts/lib/step/config.js invalidReason), so "no upper bound" is the
-- ABSENCE of the declared _max, and those seqs read INFO in the converted classification exactly as before.
-- seqs: 22, 28, 30, 34, 37, 44, 47, 48, 50, 53, 54, 55, 56, 58, 65, 66, 67, 70, 71, 74, 75, 76, 77, 78, 79, 80, 81, 82, 83, 88, 91, 94, 96.
-- The 36 lifecycle_band_* phase bands are not copied: operator y 2026-10-19 Q-ALPD-1 retires them (validated, never
-- read since 2026-05-19; ALPD-D2).
--
-- Each new row carries the OLD row's live value (an operator-set value survives), falling back to the seed default
-- when the old row is absent. The OLD rows STAY: commit ② lands at stage compute_ported, so the legacy shell is still
-- the live step and reads them until the ③ cutover, whose migration deletes them and moves the names into
-- config.retired (Spec 124 R-A).
--
-- ORDERING (trap 7): the legacy script reads the OLD names, which this migration leaves in place, so a PRE captured on
-- the legacy shell stays valid after it is applied.
--
-- Idempotent: ON CONFLICT (variable_key) DO NOTHING preserves an already-present new row.
--
-- SPEC LINK: docs/specs/01-pipeline/124_step_standard_policy.md (R-DE (v), R-DF EXTERNALIZED)
-- SPEC LINK: docs/specs/01-pipeline/84_lifecycle_phase_engine.md §3.4

-- UP
