    ('assert_lifecycle_phase_distribution_unclassified_max', 'lifecycle_unclassified_max', 100::numeric, 'assert_lifecycle_phase_distribution: Maximum number of non-terminal permits/CoAs with a NULL lifecycle_phase before assert-lifecycle-phase-distribution emits a FAIL (strongest correctness gate). Copied from lifecycle_unclassified_max (migration 288, R-DE (v)), value carried; the legacy name retires at ③.'),
    ('assert_lifecycle_phase_distribution_live_status_null_warn_count', 'lifecycle_live_status_null_warn_count', 50::numeric, 'assert_lifecycle_phase_distribution: WARN threshold for the additive breakout counters in assert-lifecycle-phase-distribution: live_status_null_count (NULL phase + non-dead status + matched_rule IS NULL) and never_classified_count (lifecycle_classified_at IS NULL). Both are dirty-queue drain-lag signals that clear on the next in-chain classify run (per docs/reports/pipeline-validation/2026-07-07-lifecycle-null-trace.md). Default 50 sits above steady-state noise (~1) and below a single day''s new-permit load (~500). Copied from lifecycle_live_status_null_warn_count (migration 288, R-DE (v)), value carried; the legacy name retires at ③.'),
    ('assert_lifecycle_phase_distribution_seq_unclassified_max', 'lifecycle_seq_unclassified_max', 5000::numeric, 'assert_lifecycle_phase_distribution: Max row count where lifecycle_seq IS NULL on permits or coa_applications. WARN threshold (E.4); Phase D + E.2 first-run state expected to violate. Tighten via E.5 after ramp-up. Copied from lifecycle_seq_unclassified_max (migration 288, R-DE (v)), value carried; the legacy name retires at ③.'),
